\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thy kingdom come, O God,
\par Thy rule, O Christ, begin;
\par Break with Thine iron rod
\par The tyrannies of sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Where is Thy reign of peace,
\par And purity, and love?
\par When shall all hatred cease,
\par As in the realms above?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When comes the promised time
\par That war shall be no more-
\par Oppressin, lust, and crime
\par Shall flee Thy face before?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. We pray Thee, Lord, arise,
\par And come in Thy great might;
\par Revive our longing eyes,
\par Which languish for Thy sight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Men scorn Thy sacred name,
\par And wolves devour Thy fold;
\par By many deeds of shame
\par We learn that love grows cold.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O'er heathen lands afar
\par Thick darkness broodeth yet:
\par Arise, O morning Star,
\par Arise, and never set!
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

